  "term": "foreshortening",
  "definition": "Foreshortening is the seeming shortening of stretches of time, especially in retrospect. In the passage, it refers to how later years can feel compressed because memory of them is more monotonous and simplified, though time can also seem to pass quickly in the moment when attention is absorbed by what is happening.",
